    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Calculate $f^{\\prime}(x)$ if $f(x)=8 \\sin{\\left(8 x - 11 \\right)}.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function\n\n$$\nf=8 \\sin{\\left(u \\right)}, \\qquad u=8 x - 11.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}=8 \\cos{\\left(u \\right)},\\qquad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=8.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}x}&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\cdot\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\\\&=(8 \\cos{\\left(u \\right)})\\cdot(8)\\\\&=64 \\cos{\\left(u \\right)}\\\\&=64 \\cos{\\left(8 x - 11 \\right)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
